        "original_id": "7110612d-811a-55bd-bf87-ee86aad4819b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Valparaiso University, Old Dominion University, College of William & Mary, Concordia Seminary, Philippine Christian University\n- People: Oswald Hoffmann\n- Places: Valparaiso, Indiana, Norfolk, Virginia, Hampton Roads, Manila, the Philippines\n- Concepts: university enrollment, honorary degrees, satellite campuses\n\nFacts:\n- Old Dominion University was established in 1930 as the Norfolk Division of the College of William & Mary.\n- Old Dominion University is a public, co-educational research university located in Norfolk, Virginia, in the United States, and it has two satellite campuses in the Hampton Roads area.\n- Old Dominion University enrolled 24,670 students in the 2014–2015 academic year, making it one of the largest universities in Virginia.\n- Valparaiso University, commonly known as Valpo, is a coeducational four-year Lutheran institution.\n- Valparaiso University enrolls about 4,500 students from more than 50 countries on a 350-acre campus.\n- Oswald Hoffmann held an honorary Doctor of Divinity degree from Concordia Seminary.\n- Oswald Hoffmann held an honorary Doctor of Laws degree from Valparaiso University in Valparaiso, Indiana.\n- Oswald Hoffmann held an honorary Doctor of Humane Letters degree from the Philippine Christian University in Manila, the Philippines.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "222d9c4f-501d-5a15-8ddb-f2eb97bead87",
        "text": "Page: Valparaiso University. Sentence: Commonly known as Valpo, the university is a coed, four-year, Lutheran institution that enrolls about 4,500 students from over 50 countries on a campus of 350 acre .\nPage: Old Dominion University. Sentence: Old Dominion University, also known as ODU, is a public, co-educational research university located in Norfolk, Virginia, United States, with two satellite campuses in the Hampton Roads area.\nPage: Old Dominion University. Sentence: It was established in 1930 as the Norfolk Division of the College of William & Mary and is now one of the largest universities in Virginia with an enrollment of 24,670 students for the 2014-2015 academic year.\nPage: Oswald Hoffmann. Sentence: In addition, he held an honorary Doctor of Divinity degree from Concordia Seminary, an honorary Doctor of Laws degree from Valparaiso University in Valparaiso, Indiana, and an honorary Doctor of Humane Letters degree from the Philippine Christian University in Manila, The Philippines.",
